From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:59:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: show the system edit menu for text

Long-pressing text in a page selected a word and nothing else, so there
was no way to copy text with touch: Blink asks for a context menu, but
ContentContextMenuController only shows the embedder's menu, and Chrome
builds menus for links and images only. RenderWidgetUIView has no edit
menu of its own ("Needs an edit menu implementation").

When a context menu request has no link and no image but has selected
text or comes from a text field, show the system edit menu
(UIEditMenuInteraction) instead, next to the selection. It offers
UIKit's own Cut, Copy, Paste and Select All commands, so their titles
are localized, filtered by the request's edit flags (Paste also needs
text on the pasteboard). They go through the responder chain to
RenderWidgetUIView, which runs them as Blink edit commands.

Status: verified at Chromium 4558926c in the iOS 27 simulator: a long
press on a word of text shows Copy and Select All, and Copy puts the
word on the system pasteboard; in a text field it shows Cut, Copy,
Paste and Select All, and Paste replaces the word; Select All selects
the page and keeps the menu, and Copy then copies all of its text. A
long press on a link still shows Chrome's link menu.

